# Sign-in flow (Auth:Mode = Accounts), runnable from Visual Studio.
# Development runs with Auth:Mode = None until the UI has sign-in screens (roadmap 0.1d). To try these requests,
# set "Auth:Mode": "Accounts" in the API's user secrets and restart it.

@host = https://localhost:3001
@tab = http-file-tab

### Which screens the UI shows: mode (Accounts/None) and sign-up (Open/Closed)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/settings

### Create an account (passwords: at least 10 characters)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-password-1" }

### Sign in. The browser uses ?useCookies=true and gets the session cookie; here useCookies=false returns a
### bearer token, which the requests below send.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login?useCookies=false
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-password-1" }

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Every API call needs sign-in plus the tab id header ("Not Connected" is expected: no connection yet)
GET {{host}}/api/databaseSchema/databases/not-connected
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}

### Without sign-in: 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Saved connections of the signed-in user (with Auth:Mode None: the local user's)
GET {{host}}/api/savedConnections
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}

### Save a connection (rememberPassword false: no password is kept)
# @name saved
POST {{host}}/api/savedConnections
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Local dev", "serverType": "PostgreSQL", "serverName": "localhost", "port": 5432, "databaseName": "postgres", "userName": "postgres", "color": "#16a34a", "rememberPassword": false }

### Change it (all fields; color null = automatic)
PUT {{host}}/api/savedConnections/{{saved.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Local dev", "serverType": "PostgreSQL", "serverName": "localhost", "port": 5433, "databaseName": null, "userName": "postgres", "color": null, "rememberPassword": false }

### Save one that remembers its password (only when SavedConnections:PasswordKey is set; otherwise 400)
# @name savedWithPassword
POST {{host}}/api/savedConnections
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Local dev (remembered)", "serverType": "PostgreSQL", "serverName": "localhost", "port": 5432, "databaseName": "postgres", "userName": "postgres", "color": null, "rememberPassword": true, "password": "…" }

### Connect with the remembered password (empty password plus the saved connection's id)
POST {{host}}/api/databaseConnection/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "serverType": "PostgreSQL", "serverName": "localhost", "port": 5432, "userName": "postgres", "password": "", "savedConnectionId": "{{savedWithPassword.response.body.$.id}}" }

### Forget the remembered password (the saved connection stays)
DELETE {{host}}/api/savedConnections/{{savedWithPassword.response.body.$.id}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}

### Delete it
DELETE {{host}}/api/savedConnections/{{saved.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}

### Connect, opening a given database (no database: the server's default, PostgreSQL: named like the user)
POST {{host}}/api/databaseConnection/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "serverType": "PostgreSQL", "serverName": "localhost", "port": 5432, "userName": "postgres", "password": "…", "databaseName": "postgres" }
